Read and follow the common brief at C:\Users\mariu\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\C--Users-mariu\8f3352b3-40ab-4151-abc9-d1de1978973c\scratchpad\common.txt (read it first, fully). You are R2. CARGO_TARGET_DIR=C:/Users/mariu/nm-target-r2. You own NEW files src/cognition.rs and src/bin/r2_*.rs only.

TASK: Cognitive skills: creativity, logic/science, design/UI-UX, business planning, marketing. Build a SEEDED multi-domain world inside your own module/binary (do not modify sim.rs): domains {coding, science, design/ui-ux, business, marketing} x skills, agents with hidden per-domain/per-approach skill, multi-step tasks (plan -> build -> critique). Some domains reward DIVERSITY (creative: value = quality x novelty vs a window of recent solutions) and others CORRECTNESS (logic/science: a verification/critic step catches errors with critic-dependent reliability). Mechanisms to test (all implement or wrap the Router trait, opt-in):
1) MAP-Elites style quality-diversity archive of agent x approach niches for routing in creative domains;
2) novelty bonus applied ONLY to creative domains (and, as a control, applied to ALL domains, and applied in a world variant where novelty has no value) — must show it does not hurt/help where it shouldn't;
3) generator->critic sequencing for logic domains with critic agent chosen by learned reliability (compare to random critic, fixed critic, no critic);
4) domain-hierarchical routing (domain -> specialist) vs flat routing.
Compare against fair baselines {keyword, eps-greedy, pooled-thompson, hebbian-robust, warm(hebbian-robust)} on the SAME world, with drift in at least one world variant. Use at least 2 world variants (e.g. different skill structure, noise level) and a rigged-check variant. Write results/r2_cognition.json. Be careful the world is not built so the new mechanism trivially wins; document world assumptions on the board. Optional (security rule applies): pyribs may be audited and used only to cross-check MAP-Elites archive behaviour; otherwise no packages.
